From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: add Skip_CAC and Uplink_CSA data-model parameters

Replace hardcoded uplink_csa/skip_cac values with data-model-controlled
parameters so they can be configured via ubus-cli:

  WiFi.Radio.{i}.Skip_CAC=1      -> writes skip_cac=1  in hostapd config
  WiFi.Radio.{i}.Uplink_CSA=1    -> writes uplink_csa=1 in hostapd config
  WiFi.EndPoint.{i}.Uplink_CSA=1 -> writes uplink_csa=1 in wpa_supplicant config

Both keys are only written when the DM param is true -- omitting the key
is equivalent to disabled in hostapd/wpa_supplicant.

Default values:
  Radio.Skip_CAC      = true   (preserves existing unconditional behaviour)
  Radio.Uplink_CSA    = false
  EndPoint.Uplink_CSA = false

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
